 "about_text": "REDCAT (the Roy and Edna Disney CalArts Theater) is CalArts' downtown Los Angeles center for contemporary visual and performing arts, opened in November 2003 inside the Walt Disney Concert Hall complex designed by Frank Gehry. Initiated by Roy E. Disney as a gift from the Walt Disney Company and matched by Roy and Patty Disney, it houses a 250-seat black-box theater, a 3,000-square-foot gallery, and a lounge. Through performances, exhibitions, screenings, and literary events, REDCAT presents experimental and cutting-edge work by Los Angeles-based and international artists, extending CalArts' mission of experimentation, discovery, and civic discourse to a professional venue in the city's downtown cultural corridor.",
